{"agent":"regen2","data":{"by":"regen2","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_SENTENCE_END.finditer(text, 0, room)` stops at index `room`, so a sentence whose period/semicolon is the last character inside `room` is not matched because the following whitespace is at index `room` and is outside `endpos`. For example, `text = \"A \" + \"B\"*113 + \". \" + \"C\"*200` has length > 120 and `room == 116`; the period is at index 115, followed by the space at index 116. `finditer(..., 0, 116)` returns no sentence-end match, so `_listed` falls back to `text[:116].rsplit(\" \", 1)[0]`, which is `\"A\"`. It therefore returns `\"A ...\"` even though the available sentence boundary would allow the advertised help to keep the much fuller `\"A \" + \"B\"*113 + \". ...\"`. The function claims to cut at the last sentence end that fits, but the off-by-one `endpos` misses the boundary case.","digest":"c13b6ce888de8034","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/family_schema.py:_listed","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/family_schema.py:_listed"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The assertion `full.startswith(listed.removesuffix(FS.CUT_MARK))` does not require `listed` to actually contain `FS.CUT_MARK`. Given a bad but plausible `family_entry` implementation that sets the listed description to `full[:FS.LISTED_TEXT_MAX]` without appending the cut marker, the loop’s length check passes and this assertion still passes because `removesuffix` is a no-op and the truncated string is a prefix of `full`. Since the companion test exercises `FS._listed` directly but not the generated family-entry path, the generated MCP family schema could lose the “it was cut” marker while both new tests remain green. Add an explicit `listed.endswith(FS.CUT_MARK)` or assert `listed == FS._listed(full)` to pin the actual listing behavior.","digest":"ab14d6686742e7ae","location":"tests/test_mcp_families.py:test_a_listed_argument_text_stays_short_and_says_when_it_was_cut","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_mcp_families.py:test_a_listed_argument_text_stays_short_and_says_when_it_was_cut"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":0,"delta_from":"5284744d5f43a8b02ea4b1f03ae4230cdd244e2f","delta_raised":[],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":2064,"diff_sha":"0e4759f1b21c62a5571f4751fa953a5d909bce33e960c4eb5ca3b3a64facb54c","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 5284744d5f","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":216.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"full_coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"aaf165b9d61e4d60","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B66b0d8218e-2.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261105T003503Z-1dee4511.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"b32b4bf6a7d57ef969492ce76b1ff0d573d0a706","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/surfaces/tools/family_schema.py":"100644 e0f0bfb5b062feca2a827295df731c2a86612069","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.surfaces.tools.family_schema.toml":"100644 c4cebce7ba2467e8170c12d5a0577e802f23d723","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr":"100644 e073aad262bd8e55f266c04e50f2dd7dadfba459","tests/test_mcp_families.py":"100644 8991bec58fc571a4b192e99d3987eb3e6bf45b73"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round_kept":true,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/tools/family_schema.py:_listed","tests/test_mcp_families.py:test_a_listed_argument_text_stays_short_and_says_when_it_was_cut"],"tree_sha":"b32b4bf6a7d5+clean","unavailable_deltas":[{"at":"2026-11-05T05:43:04Z","diff_chars":0,"reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM before a reviewer finished: nothing was reviewed, which is not a pass","reviewer":""}],"unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":""},"id":"e7d654551ea0e992d41c96951","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":138772,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B66b0d8218e-2